💀 **KILLFILE INITIATED**  
Title: `KillGamingServices.ps1`  
Function: Annihilate Microsoft Gaming Services, purge registry roots, kill hidden overlay triggers, and disable scheduled reactivation attempts.

---

### 📜 PowerShell — Step 1: Create the File  
Run this block in PowerShell:

````powershell
New-Item -Path "$env:USERPROFILE\Desktop\KillGamingServices.ps1" -ItemType File -Force
````

---

### 📥 PowerShell — Step 2: Fill the File with This Purge Script

````powershell
Set-Content -Path "$env:USERPROFILE\Desktop\KillGamingServices.ps1" -Value @'
Write-Host "🗡️ Killing Microsoft Gaming Services..." -ForegroundColor Red

# 1. Remove AppxPackage for all users
try {
    Get-AppxPackage Microsoft.GamingServices | Remove-AppxPackage -AllUsers -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    Write-Host "✔️ AppxPackage removed"
} catch {
    Write-Host "⚠️ Failed to remove AppxPackage (may already be gone)"
}

# 2. Remove registry service keys
$regPaths = @(
    "HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\GamingServices",
    "HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\GamingServicesNet"
)
foreach ($path in $regPaths) {
    if (Test-Path $path) {
        Remove-Item -Path $path -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
        Write-Host "✔️ Registry key removed: $path"
    } else {
        Write-Host "⛔ Registry key not found: $path"
    }
}

# 3. Kill scheduled tasks
$tasks = Get-ScheduledTask | Where-Object { $_.TaskName -like "*GamingServices*" }
foreach ($task in $tasks) {
    Disable-ScheduledTask -TaskName $task.TaskName -TaskPath $task.TaskPath -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    Write-Host "✔️ Scheduled Task disabled: $($task.TaskName)"
}

# 4. Stop ghost services if still alive
$services = Get-Service | Where-Object { $_.Name -like "*GamingServices*" }
foreach ($svc in $services) {
    try {
        Stop-Service -Name $svc.Name -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
        Write-Host "✔️ Stopped service: $($svc.Name)"
    } catch {
        Write-Host "⚠️ Could not stop service: $($svc.Name)"
    }
}

Write-Host "`n🔥 KILLFILE COMPLETE — GamingServices annihilated. REBOOT NOW." -ForegroundColor Green
'@
````

---

### ✅ Final Step: Run as Admin

1. Go to Desktop
2. Right-click `KillGamingServices.ps1`
3. Choose **“Run with PowerShell (Admin)”**

System will clean and drop out of injected focus overlays.

